+  finding: 'The cleaner and the backstop both depend on the one-line form ''- Fails if: text''. Run on
+    a nested form (''- Fails if:'' followed by indented ''- A ...'' bullets) without_fails_if drops only
+    the header line and leaves the child bullets in the clean copy, and fails_if_texts finds no text for
+    the backstop, so SE-3 (grep for the words) and check_drafts are both blind. Tested by calling without_fails_if
+    on that input. The bold-label form (''**Fails if:**'' + bullets) over-removes: it also drops the next
+    sibling bullet (for example a Limit line), which fails closed but loses story content. The template
+    form is single-line, so this is a robustness gap, not a hit on today''s pages.'
