new file mode 100644
index 00000000..0ed5beb3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/components/plays/shape-plan/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,550 @@
+---
+name: shape-plan
+position: both
+argument-hint: "<business intent issue number>"
+description: 'Make the one plan of a business intent that /shape-slice has served with a slice, or bring it up to date — the second play of the shaping loop (ADR 049: /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval). Run as /shape-plan <intent-issue> (for example /shape-plan 788). It holds every slice the spine links to the intent, and for each slice it makes one epic (an issue of type Feature, no label) and one story for each feature (an issue of type Story, no label, a sub-issue of the epic), each story written from its feature''s ICE and that feature''s capability''s ICE: its scope of work (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance, with no failure condition and no recovery condition. It finds before it makes: an epic or a story that the plan file marks with represents is used and never made again, and a found story only gains the sections it lacks, keeping every line a person wrote. A feature that left the slice has its story moved out of the plan, and the story stays open in the tracker; a feature whose ICE is not ready is skipped and named. The epic holds the feature-to-story map, which always agrees with the plan file''s tree. Nothing reaches the tracker and the plan file is not written before the product owner types yes at one pinned checkpoint, after a brief that shows every write. Writes only the plan file, the epics and the stories; nothing in the evals folder or the product model. Position both: it opens its own change and lands it through commit-change, propose-change, check-change and merge-change, on the plan''s branch when the intent has one.'
+user-invocable: true
+---
+
+# shape-plan
+
+A person names a business intent that `/shape-slice` has served with a slice. /shape-plan
+makes the intent's **one plan**, or brings it up to date: the plan file
+(`.garura/project/plans/<intent-issue>.yaml`), one **epic** for each slice the plan holds, and
+one **story** for each feature of that slice. Each story is written from its feature's ICE and
+that feature's capability's ICE, and holds no failure condition and no recovery condition:
+those stay in the slice's hidden file, which `/shape-slice` wrote. A second run makes no
+copies. The eval play (#798) comes next, once it is built.
+
+The run reads the slices from the spine (the link "slice serves business intent"); it never
+picks, orders or tests a slice. It finds each epic and story that already stands for a slice or
+a feature before it makes one, by the plan file's `represents` marks, never by a title. It
+shows the product owner one brief with every tracker write and the plan-file change, and
+writes nothing before the typed yes.
+
+**Pipeline position: both.** start-change opens the change at the head (on the plan's
+sub-branch when the intent has a plan); the end sequence commit-change → propose-change →
+check-change → merge-change lands it.
+
+## Compiled From
+
+This play was compiled from the shape-plan ICE (`reference/ice.md`) by create-play. Intent
+defines constraints (C1–C13) and failure conditions (F1–F11); the expectation defines success
+scenarios (S1–S7), a Done means (D1–D5, baked to `stop-condition.yaml`), and one recovery entry
+per failure condition. To modify this play, update `reference/ice.md` and recompile with
+edit-play.
+Do NOT edit this file manually — it is a compiled artifact.
+
+## Role
+
+You are the orchestrator. You own the step order, the one brief and the checkpoint. The play
+reads no memory itself. The `product-os-keeper` agent gathers context and calls the skill
+`author-work-items`, which writes the words of each epic and story; the agent passes the
+skill's output on as it is and never writes content. `template-manager` hands out the approval
+prompt and the close templates. You run all mechanical work through bundled scripts: the
+gather and the clean ICE copies (`gather_plan.py`, which runs the ready check
+`check_ice_workable.py`), the find (`find_work_items.py`), the draft check (`check_drafts.py`),
+the brief (`render_brief.py`), the checkpoint record and the write gate (`record_approval.py`),
+the tracker writes (`write_work_items.py`, through `platform_adapter.py`), the plan file
+(`write_plan_file.py`), the checks (`check_plan.py`, `check_tracker.py`), the write guard
+(`scoped_write_guard.py`) and the stop condition. Every script writes its files through a
+temp file and a rename (`plan_common.py`). The play never writes the plan file, an epic or a
+story by hand.
+
+**Forbidden:** a second plan for one intent (C1); picking, ordering or testing a slice, or
+leaving out a slice the spine links to the intent (C2); matching a work item by its title, or
+making an epic or a story that the plan file already marks (C3); deleting a story whose
+feature left the slice, or leaving it in the plan (C4); reading a "Fails if" line, or a story,
+an epic or a plan file that holds a failure or recovery condition (C5); an epic title that
+says how the product is built, or a map that disagrees with the tree (C6); writing outside the
+plan file, the epics and the stories — the evals folder and the product model above all (C7);
+a tracker write before the typed yes, a write the brief did not show, or a checkpoint skipped
+by config (C8); a story built from an ICE that is not ready, or a skipped feature not named
+(C9); landing outside the change plays or on the wrong branch (C10); a real person's name, or
+text a person cannot follow (C11); rewriting or deleting a line a person wrote on a found story
+(C12); a label on an epic or a story, or a wrong issue type (C13).
+
+**Agent boundaries:**
+
+| Agent | Domain | Skills it uses | Phases |
+|-------|--------|----------------|--------|
+| `product-os-keeper` | Gather context and pass it on: hand the skill only `skill-input.json` and the clean ICE copies it names (never `gather.json`, never an ICE page), check that no clean copy holds a failure line, call the skill, and pass its `drafts.json` on as it is | `author-work-items` | Draft |
+| `template-manager` (utility) | Hand out the approval prompt and the close templates (evidence file, delivery report, Next-line map) into short-term memory | — | Checkpoint, Close |
+
+`product-os-keeper` is the single **domain agent**; `template-manager` is the one utility
+agent. The skill `author-work-items` was built for this play. The start and end sequence are
+injected sub-plays; everything else is a script.
+
+## Pre-flight
+
+| Check | Constraint | Action on Failure |
+|-------|-----------|-------------------|
+| Resolve config, `stm_base`, `product_base` (`.garura/core/config.yaml`) | — | Hard halt |
+| A business intent issue number was given (`/shape-plan <intent-issue>`, digits only); the plan's ID is that number | C1 | Hard halt — ask for the intent's issue number |
+| The product model's spine exists (`<product_base>product-os/_spine.yaml`) | C2 | Hard halt — run `/shape-slice <intent-issue>` first |
+| **Clean model tree** — after Step 0: `git status --porcelain -- <product_base>product-os` is empty | C7 | Hard halt (REC7) |
+| **Clean plans tree** — after Step 0: `git status --porcelain -- .garura/project/plans` is empty, so the write guard sees only this run's change and a restore never takes back a person's own plan edits | C7, C8 | Hard halt (REC7) |
+
+Resolve the facts with the bundled resolver, not by inference:
+
+```
+git branch --show-current
+python3 scripts/preflight.py --play shape-plan --config .garura/core/config.yaml \
+    --branch "<current branch>"
+```
+
+`preflight.py` gives `stm_base`, `product_base` and `evidence_record`. The change's own issue
+comes from start-change (Step 0), not from the branch name: the intent issue and the change
+issue are two issues. After Step 0, with `<issue>` = the change issue:
+
+```
+python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase start \
+    --marker "{stm_base}<issue>/status/session-stamp-shape-plan.json" \
+    --cwd "$(pwd)" --branch "$(git branch --show-current)"
+git rev-parse HEAD > {stm_base}<issue>/context/shape-plan/start-sha.txt
+shasum -a 256 .garura/project/plans/<intent-issue>.yaml > {stm_base}<issue>/context/shape-plan/plan-before.txt \
+    || echo "no plan file" > {stm_base}<issue>/context/shape-plan/plan-before.txt
+```
+
+Names used below: `<intent>` = `bi-<intent-issue>`, `<id>` = `<intent-issue>` (the plan's ID),
+`<model>` = `<product_base>product-os`, `<plans>` = `.garura/project/plans`,
+`<plan-file>` = `<plans>/<id>.yaml`, `<working>` = `{stm_base}<issue>/context/shape-plan/`.
+The stop condition reads `{stm_base}<issue>/`.
+
+**Resume check:** if `{stm_base}<issue>/status/shape-plan.json` exists, resume — skip
+completed steps, reset an in-progress step to pending, continue from the first incomplete one.
+
+## Task DAG
+
+Create ALL tasks right after pre-flight, before any domain work. The play owns this DAG.
+
+```
+[T0]  start-change (injected — start)                          blockedBy: []
+[T1]  Gather the slices and the clean ICE copies                blockedBy: [T0]
+[T2]  Find the epics and stories that exist                     blockedBy: [T1]
+[T3]  Draft the epics and stories                               blockedBy: [T2]
+[T4]  Check the drafts                                          blockedBy: [T3]
+[T5]  The brief and the checkpoint (yes / change / stop)        blockedBy: [T4]
+[T6]  Write the epics and stories in the tracker                blockedBy: [T5]
+[T7]  Write the plan file                                       blockedBy: [T6]
+[T8]  Check the plan, the tracker and the writes                blockedBy: [T7]
+[T9]  Commit the plan file                                      blockedBy: [T8]
+[E1]  commit-change (injected — end)                            blockedBy: [T9]
+[E2]  propose-change (injected — end)                           blockedBy: [E1]
+[E3]  check-change (injected — end)                             blockedBy: [E2]
+[E4]  merge-change (injected — end)                             blockedBy: [E3]
+[T10] Scenario Validation                                       blockedBy: [E4]
+[T11] Close                                                     blockedBy: [T10]
+```
+
+Mark each task in progress before its step and completed right after its eval passes. No
+runtime reordering. A **change** at the checkpoint sends the run back to T3; T3–T5 run again
+in order.
+
+## Workflow
+
+### Phase: Start (injected — D2 position: both, head)
+
+**Step 0 — start-change** · Owner: `start-change` (sub-play) · Depends on: pre-flight
+Run the start-of-pipeline member as a sub-play with `parent_run_id`. It resolves or creates
+the change issue, cuts its branch (the plan's sub-branch when the intent has a plan file,
+`<plans>/<id>.yaml`), and inits short-term memory. Then assert the clean model tree and the
+clean plans tree (hard halt if dirty — REC7).
+
+    { "play": "start-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>",
+      "inputs":  { "title": "[TASK] shape-plan: make the plan for business intent #<intent-issue>" },
+      "outputs": { "result": "<working>start-change.json" } }
+
+### Phase: Gather
+
+**Step 1 — Gather the slices and the clean ICE copies** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 0
+
+```
+python3 scripts/gather_plan.py --root <model> --spine <model>/_spine.yaml --intent <intent> \
+    --plans <plans> --out <working>gather.json
+```
+
+It lists every slice whose `intents` lists the intent, in the spine's order (C2), each
+slice's features in build order, each feature's capability and the pages of its two ICE. It
+runs the ready check (`check_ice_workable.py`) on both ICE of each feature: a feature whose
+ICE is not ready is `ready: false` with its `reason`, and gets no clean copy (C9). For each
+ready feature it writes `<working>ice/<feature id>.md`: both ICE with every "Fails if" block
+taken out — the line and every line under it, nested bullets and wrapped text included (C5).
+It also writes `<working>skill-input.json`: each slice's id, name and outcome, and each ready
+feature's id, name, one line and clean copy's path — no ICE page path. The skill reads only
+`skill-input.json` and the clean copies, never `gather.json` or an ICE page. Exit 2
+means no slice serves the intent: tell the person to run `/shape-slice <intent-issue>` first,
+and close HALTED.
+**SE-1 (F2/C1/C2):** `gather.json` `plan_id` equals `<intent-issue>` and `plan_file` is
+`<plans>/<id>.yaml`, the one plan file for the intent; its `slices` are every spine slice whose
+`intents` lists `<intent>`, in spine order, none left out and none added.
+**SE-2 (F8/C9):** each feature with `ready: false` has a `reason` that is not empty and a null
+`clean_ice`; each feature with `ready: true` has a `clean_ice` file on disk; no other file is
+in `<working>ice/`.
+**SE-3 (F3/C5):** `grep -ril "fails if" <working>ice/` finds nothing; no line of a "Fails if"
+block of a feature's two ICE (children included) is in its clean copy; and neither
+`skill-input.json` nor a clean copy names an ICE page (`grep -l "feature.md\|capability.md\|ice.md"`
+over them finds nothing).
+
+### Phase: Find
+
+**Step 2 — Find the epics and stories that exist** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 1
+
+```
+python3 scripts/find_work_items.py --gather <working>gather.json --plan-file <plan-file> \
+    --out <working>work-items.json
+```
+
+It reads the plan file and, through the code-host adapter, the tracker; it writes nothing.
+An epic is `use` when a node of the tree has `represents: <slice id>`, else `make`; a story is
+`use`, `add-sections` (it lacks "Scope of work" or "Context guidance"), `make`, or `skip` (its
+feature is not ready). It never compares titles (C3). `move_out` lists each marked story whose
+feature is no longer in the slice (C4). Exit 1 lists a duplicate (two nodes stand for one
+slice, or for one feature in one epic) or a marked issue the tracker does not have: show it to
+the person in plain words and stop (REC2); the run goes on only after the person fixes the
+plan file.
+**SE-4 (F2/C3):** `work-items.json` reads `ok: true`; its `duplicates` is empty; each `use` or
+`add-sections` item's issue is the `issue` of the plan-file node whose `represents` names that
+slice or feature; no item with a marked node is `make`.
+**SE-5 (F6/C4):** each node under an epic whose `represents` names a feature that is not in the
+slice is in that slice's `move_out`, and no feature of the slice is.
+
+### Phase: Draft
+
+**Step 3 — Draft the epics and stories** · Owner: `product-os-keeper` · Depends on: Step 2
+
+    { "task":    "have the epic of each slice and one story for each ready feature drafted. Hand author-work-items only skill-input.json and the clean ICE copies it names (clean_ice); never open or hand on gather.json or any ICE page. First check that no clean copy holds the words 'Fails if' (grep -il 'fails if' on each); if one does, stop with step_failure and name it. Call author-work-items with skill_input, the clean copies, and, on a re-run, the problems of drafts-check.json (fix mode) or the product owner's change (change mode) with the earlier drafts.json. Pass its drafts.json on as it is. Gather and pass on only; the skill writes every word",
+      "inputs":  { "skill_input": "<working>skill-input.json", "clean_ice": "<working>ice/",
+                   "problems": "<working>drafts-check.json, on a fix", "change": "<the product owner's change, on a re-run>",
+                   "drafts": "<working>drafts.json, on a re-run" },
+      "outputs": { "drafts": "<working>drafts.json" },
+      "skills":  ["author-work-items"],
+      "task_id": "shape-plan-draft" }
+
+**Step 4 — Check the drafts** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 3
+
+```
+python3 scripts/check_drafts.py --drafts <working>drafts.json --gather <working>gather.json \
+    --out <working>drafts-check.json
+```
+
+It reads the original ICE pages itself, so the "Fails if" lines reach no skill and no person,
+and compares the drafts with every line of each "Fails if" block, children included.
+Exit 1 lists each problem by slice and feature: send `drafts-check.json` back to the
+`shape-plan-draft` contract (fix mode), then run Step 4 again (REC3). The run does not go on
+until it reads ok.
+**SE-6 (F3/C5/C6):** `drafts-check.json` reads `ok: true`: each slice has an epic title; no
+text of an epic or a story holds a line of a "Fails if" block of its two ICE, the words
+"Fails if", or a recovery phrase; each story has goals, limits, expectations and the four Context guidance
+lines.
+**SE-7 (F1/C9):** in `drafts.json`, each ready feature of each slice has exactly one story, and
+no story is for a feature that is not ready or not in its slice.
+
+### Phase: Checkpoint (class: one-way-door, pinned)
+
+**Step 5 — The brief and the checkpoint** · Owner: play (+ `template-manager` for the approval prompt) · Depends on: Step 4 · Checkpoint (class: one-way-door, **pinned** — the product owner decides; never skipped by config, `standards/rules/gate-config.md`)
+
+```
+python3 scripts/render_brief.py --gather <working>gather.json \
+    --work-items <working>work-items.json --drafts <working>drafts.json \
+    --out <working>brief.md
+```
+
+The script builds the whole brief from the run's records, so no write can be left out (C8):
+each epic and story the run will make, use, add sections to or move out, with the text a new
+item or section gets and each type, label or sub-issue change; the plan-file change; and each
+skipped feature with its reason (C9). The brief is never edited by hand: a problem in it goes
+back to the step whose record it reads. Frame the brief with the approval prompt from
+`template-manager` (`standards/templates/approval-prompt.md`) and show it. Ask the product
+owner to type **yes**, **change: <what>**, or **stop**. Save the reply word for word, and
+record it with the files the person saw, so the yes stays tied to them (their sha256):
+
+```
+python3 scripts/record_approval.py --decision <yes|change|stop> --reply "<their exact words>" \
+    --at <now, UTC> --brief <working>brief.md --work-items <working>work-items.json \
+    --drafts <working>drafts.json --out <working>approval.json
+```
+
+- **yes** → Step 6.
+- **change** → nothing was written; re-run Step 3 with the change (change mode), then Steps 4
+  and 5; show the brief again.
+- **stop** → nothing was written, and nothing is written now. Write
+  `git status --porcelain -- <plans>` to `<working>stop-check.txt`, and
+  `shasum -a 256 <plan-file>` (or "no plan file") to `<working>plan-after-stop.txt`; close
+  HALTED. A stop needs no undo; if any write is found after a stop, undo it with
+  `scoped_write_guard.py --product-base <product_base> --base-ref HEAD --also-tree .garura/project/plans --restore --out <working>guard-restore.json`
+  and REC5.
+**SE-8 (F5/C8):** `approval.json` holds the product owner's typed words and the sha256 of
+`brief.md`, `work-items.json` and `drafts.json` as shown; `brief.md` names every
+epic and story in `work-items.json` with its action, and every `move_out`; no
+`tracker-record.json` exists before `approval.json` reads `decision: yes`; after a stop,
+`stop-check.txt` is empty, `plan-after-stop.txt` equals `plan-before.txt`, and there is no
+`tracker-record.json`.
+**SE-9 (F8/C9):** each feature with `ready: false` in `gather.json` is in `brief.md`'s
+"Skipped features" with its reason.
+**SE-10 (F10/C11):** `brief.md`, `drafts.json` and the plan file use personas and plain words
+(ASD-STE100) and name no real person — `grep -i "$(git config user.name)"` over them finds
+nothing.
+
+### Phase: Write
+
+**Step 6 — Write the epics and stories in the tracker** · Owner: play (scripts) · Depends on: Step 5 (yes)
+The gate runs right before the first tracker write; any exit but 0 stops here, and nothing
+reaches the tracker (C8):
+
+```
+python3 scripts/record_approval.py verify --file <working>approval.json
+python3 scripts/write_work_items.py --work-items <working>work-items.json \
+    --drafts <working>drafts.json --gather <working>gather.json \
+    --approval <working>approval.json --plan-id <id> --out <working>tracker-record.json
+```
+
+`write_work_items.py` refuses again (exit 2, nothing written) unless the approval reads yes,
+and when the brief, `work-items.json` or `drafts.json` is no longer the file the person saw
+(its sha256 differs): then show the brief again (Step 5). It makes each epic as an issue of
+type Feature, and each story as an issue of type Story with its epic as parent, each in one
+write and with no label (C13); it adds each story's "Written from" line (the two ICE pages)
+from `gather.json`; on a used item it sets the type when it is wrong
+and takes off its labels; on `add-sections` it appends only the missing sections and keeps
+every line of the body (C12); it writes the epic's "Feature-to-story map" (C6); for
+`move_out` it takes the story off the epic's sub-issues and the map, and leaves it open (C4).
+Each write goes through the code-host adapter's verbs, and `tracker-record.json` is written
+after every write. Exit 1 means the tracker failed part way: the record reads `ok: false`,
+names the `failed` step and keeps every issue made before it. Still run Step 7, so the plan
+file marks those issues and the next run finds them and makes no copy; then show the record to
+the person and close HALTED (REC5).
+**SE-11 (F7/C12):** each `updated` story in `tracker-record.json` has `lines_kept: true`, and for
+each `add-sections` story every line of its body before the run is in its body now, in order.
+**SE-12 (F5/C8):** `tracker-record.json` `approval_at` equals `approval.json` `at`; the sha256 of
+`brief.md`, `work-items.json` and `drafts.json` still equals what `approval.json` recorded; each
+issue in `created`, `updated` and `moved_out` matches an item of `work-items.json` that
+`brief.md` shows.
+
+**Step 7 — Write the plan file** · Owner: play (script) · Depends on: Step 6
+
+```
+python3 scripts/write_plan_file.py --plan-file <plan-file> --gather <working>gather.json \
+    --record <working>tracker-record.json --out <working>plan-write.json
+```
+
+It also takes a record that reads `ok: false`, and marks each issue it lists. It makes the
+plan file when it is missing (`id`, `title`, `status: active`, `tree`), or
+updates it: one epic node for each slice (`represents: <slice id>`) with one story node for
+each feature of its map (`represents: <feature id>`), and moved-out story nodes taken out. It
+changes the file line by line and keeps every other node, line and comment; with nothing to
+change the file stays byte for byte the same. The plan file holds titles, issues and marks
+only: never a failure or recovery condition (C5).
+**SE-13 (F2/C1):** `plan-write.json` reads `ok: true` and its `path` is `<plan-file>`; there is
+one plan file for the intent under `<plans>`, and no slice has two epic nodes in it.
+
+### Phase: Check
+
+**Step 8 — Check the plan, the tracker and the writes** · Owner: play (scripts) · Depends on: Step 7
+
+```
+python3 scripts/check_plan.py --plan-file <plan-file> --gather <working>gather.json \
+    --record <working>tracker-record.json --out <working>plan-check.json
+python3 scripts/check_tracker.py --record <working>tracker-record.json \
+    --out <working>tracker-check.json
+python3 scripts/scoped_write_guard.py --product-base <product_base> --base-ref HEAD \
+    --also-tree .garura/project/plans --allow '.garura/project/plans/<id>.yaml' \
+    --out <working>guard-report.json
+```
+
+`check_plan.py` exit 1: a missing story node is REC1, a tree that disagrees with the map is
+REC4 — fix and run Steps 6–8 again. `check_tracker.py` exit 1: a label or a wrong type is
+REC11, a deleted or closed moved-out story is REC6. The guard's allowed set is C7's: the one
+plan file. Exit 1: re-run it with `--restore` to undo each write outside the set (REC7), then
+run Steps 7–8 again. The run writes nothing in the evals folder and nothing in the product
+model, so it makes no `feat(model)` commit.
+**SE-14 (F1/F4/C6):** `plan-check.json` reads `ok: true`: each ready feature of each slice has
+exactly one story node under its slice's epic node, no story node stands for a feature outside
+its slice, each epic's map names the same story for each feature as the tree, and each
+skipped feature is in `skipped`.
+**SE-15 (F11/C13):** `tracker-check.json` reads `ok: true`: each issue of the record exists, each
+epic has type Feature and each story type Story, none has a label, and each epic's sub-issues
+are its stories.
+**SE-16 (F6/C4):** each story in `tracker-record.json` `moved_out` is open in the tracker, is not
+a sub-issue of its epic, and is in neither the plan file's tree nor the epic's map.
+**SE-17 (F7/C7):** `guard-report.json` reads `ok: true` — no path in the product model and no
+path under `.garura/project/plans/` other than `<plan-file>` changed (the evals folder is
+untouched).
+
+### Phase: Commit
+
+**Step 9 — Commit the plan file** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 8
+The commit runs only when the recorded answer is yes and the plan file changed
+(`plan-write.json` `changed: true`); the gate runs right before it:
+
+```
+python3 scripts/record_approval.py verify --file <working>approval.json
+git add -- .garura/project/plans/<id>.yaml
+git commit -m "feat(plan): make or update plan <id> for business intent #<id> (#<issue>)"
+```
+
+### Phase: End sequence (injected — D2 position: both, tail)
+
+Each member runs as a sub-play with `parent_run_id`; each resolves its own context from the
+branch and config.
+
+**Step E1 — commit-change** · blockedBy: Step 9 — commits the run records under `{stm_base}<issue>/`.
+
+    { "play": "commit-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "<working>end/commit-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E2 — propose-change** · blockedBy: E1
+
+    { "play": "propose-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "<working>end/propose-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E3 — check-change** · blockedBy: E2 — a reject stops the chain before merge.
+
+    { "play": "check-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "<working>end/check-change.json" } }
+
+**Step E4 — merge-change** · blockedBy: E3 — lands on the plan's branch when the change sits in a plan.
+
+    { "play": "merge-change", "parent_run_id": "<this run id>", "inputs": {}, "outputs": { "result": "<working>end/merge-change.json" } }
+
+**SE-18 (F9/C10):** `start-change.json` shows the change opened by start-change; the
+`<working>end/` results are present in order; the PR's base is the plan's branch when the
+intent has a plan (else main), and `merge-change.json` reports it merged.
+
+### Phase: Scenario Validation
+
+**Step 10 — Scenario evals** · Owner: play · Depends on: E4
+- **SCE-1 (S1 — product owner, first plan):** with no plan file and one slice of three
+  features, `plan-write.json` reads `made: true`, `plan-check.json` and `tracker-check.json`
+  read `ok: true`, `tracker-record.json` `created` holds one epic and three stories, the epic's
+  map names the three stories, and `drafts-check.json` reads `ok: true`.
+- **SCE-2 (S2 — product owner, second run):** `tracker-record.json` `created` is empty,
+  `plan-write.json` reads `changed: false`, and the plan file's `shasum -a 256` equals
+  `plan-before.txt`.
+- **SCE-3 (S3 — product owner, items made by hand):** `tracker-record.json` `created` is empty;
+  each `add-sections` story is in `updated` with only `section added` changes and
+  `lines_kept: true`; `tracker-check.json` reads `ok: true`.
+- **SCE-4 (S4 — product owner, the slice changed):** `tracker-record.json` `moved_out` names the
+  story of the feature that left, `check_tracker.py` finds it open, `created` holds one story
+  for the feature that came in, and `plan-check.json` reads `ok: true`.
+- **SCE-5 (S5 — product owner, a second slice):** there is one plan file for the intent; its
+  tree has two epic nodes, one for each slice, and `tracker-record.json` `epics` names two
+  epics.
+- **SCE-6 (S6 — product owner, stop):** `approval.json` reads `decision: stop`, there is no
+  `tracker-record.json`, `stop-check.txt` is empty, and `plan-after-stop.txt` equals
+  `plan-before.txt`.
+- **SCE-7 (S7 — product owner, an ICE not ready):** `tracker-record.json` `skipped` names the
+  feature with its reason, `brief.md` names it under "Skipped features", and `plan-check.json`
+  reads `ok: true` with the feature in `skipped`.
+
+### Phase: Evidence & Close
+
+**Step 11 — Close** · Owner: play · Depends on: Step 10
+Run the Standard Play Close. The close is stop-condition gated: the baked
+`stop-condition.yaml` (D1 the plan check reads ok; D2 the approval reads yes; D3 the draft
+check reads ok; D4 the tracker check reads ok; D5 the write guard reads ok) must read **held**
+before a COMPLETED close. A stop, or a run with no slice, closes HALTED.
+
+```bash
+# --- Standard Play Close (shared; see ../_shared/play-close.md) ---
+# Run the close in ../_shared/play-close.md. Its Step L loads the templates through
+# template-manager and sets ts and evidence_dest; then run this play's own lines below;
+# then Steps C0-C2.
+#   evidence_base, slug (project-scoped play):
+#     evidence_base="${stm_base}${issue}/evidence/shape-plan/"   ; slug="#${issue}"
+# Session identity stamp (#463) — close phase; start phase ran at pre-flight
+session_stamp=$(python3 scripts/session_stamp.py --phase close \
+    --marker "${stm_base}${issue}/status/session-stamp-shape-plan.json")
+# Stop-condition gate (#464) — Step C0: this play carries a baked manifest, so the
+# gate is LIVE. Evaluate the Done means against the issue folder.
+python3 scripts/check_stop_condition.py \
+    --manifest "<play-dir>/stop-condition.yaml" \
+    --base "${stm_base}${issue}/" \
+    --out "${stm_base}${issue}/status/stop-condition-shape-plan.yaml"
+sc_exit=$?   # 0 held · 1 unmet · 2 error
+```
+
+**Step C0 — bind the verdict.** `sc_exit == 0` (held) permits `status: COMPLETED`. Anything
+else closes `HALTED` with `exit_reason: stop_condition_unmet`, and the evidence's Stop
+Condition section names every unmet clause. An unevaluable verdict is never a pass.
+
+**Step C1 — Write evidence file.** Gated by the resolved `evidence.record` flag (per-play
+`evidence.plays.shape-plan`, else global; absent ⇒ record). When false, skip the write and
+record `evidence skipped (record=false)` in the report's pointer line. Otherwise fill the
+`evidence-file.md` slots (play `shape-plan`, run_id `shape-plan-${ts}`, issue, the intent
+issue, started_at/completed_at, status per C0, exit_reason; artifacts produced: `gather.json`,
+`work-items.json`, `drafts.json`, `drafts-check.json`, `brief.md`, `approval.json`,
+`tracker-record.json` with the epics and stories made, used and moved out, `plan-write.json`
+and the plan file's path, `plan-check.json`, `tracker-check.json`, `guard-report.json`, the
+plan commit sha, and the skill the agent contract named; step and scenario eval results
+SE-1…SE-18 / SCE-1…SCE-7; the checkpoint answers in the person's words; the session identity
+stamp fields from $session_stamp (#463); and stop_condition per C0) and write to
+`$evidence_dest`. Do NOT hand-author the body.
+
+**Step C2 — Render delivery report.** Fill the `delivery-report.md` slots and output the
+report: `## shape-plan Delivered — #${issue}`, the Run Summary table, the Pipeline Steps table
+from the task DAG, the Artifacts Produced table (the plan file, each epic and story made, used,
+given sections or moved out, each skipped feature with its reason, the PR), and the **Next**
+line from the Next-line map (`$next_map`, from `template-manager`), per `play-close.md`; omit it
+when the map's command is null. Next Steps: the eval play (#798) reads the epic, its map and
+its stories once it is built. End with a pointer to `$evidence_dest`. Always emitted; never
+gated.
+
+```bash
+# --- end Standard Play Close ---
+```
+
+## Scenario Validation
+
+| Scenario | Persona | Eval |
+|----------|---------|------|
+| S1 — first plan | product owner | SCE-1 |
+| S2 — second run | product owner | SCE-2 |
+| S3 — items made by hand | product owner | SCE-3 |
+| S4 — the slice changed | product owner | SCE-4 |
+| S5 — a second slice | product owner | SCE-5 |
+| S6 — stop at the checkpoint | product owner | SCE-6 |
+| S7 — an ICE not ready | product owner | SCE-7 |
+
+## Recovery
+
+| For | Trigger | Direction | Handoff |
+|-----|---------|-----------|---------|
+| F1 | a feature of a slice the plan holds has no story, or a story in the plan stands for no feature of its slice | make the missing story; move a story that stands for no feature of its slice out of the plan | autonomous |
+| F2 | a second plan for one intent, a second epic for one slice, or a second story for one feature in one epic | keep the first plan, epic or story, move the copy out of the plan, and tell the person which one was kept | human |
+| F3 | a story, the epic or the plan file holds a failure condition or a recovery condition | take the line out and draft the story or the epic again from the two clean ICE copies | autonomous |
+| F4 | the plan file's tree and the epic's feature-to-story map disagree | write the plan file's tree and the epic's map again from the run's record, so they agree | autonomous |
+| F5 | a tracker write happened before the yes, a write the person did not see in the brief happened, or a stop left a tracker write or a plan-file change behind | undo each tracker write the record lists and put back the plan file as it was (`scoped_write_guard.py --restore`); show the brief again | human |
+| F6 | a story for a feature that left the slice was deleted, or stays in the plan | open the deleted story again, or take it out of the plan's tree and the epic's map, so it stays in the tracker and out of the plan | human |
+| F7 | the run wrote outside the plan file, the epics and the stories (the evals folder, the product model, or any other file), or a found story lost a line a person wrote | undo the write outside the allowed set (`scoped_write_guard.py --also-tree .garura/project/plans --restore`), or put back the person's line on the found story | autonomous |
+| F8 | a story was built from an ICE that is not ready, or a skipped part is not named in the brief | take back the story built from the part that is not ready, skip the part, and name it in the brief | autonomous |
+| F9 | the change landed outside the change plays, or on the wrong branch | land the change through the change plays, on the branch the target script gives | human |
+| F10 | a page names a real person, or a person cannot follow it | rewrite with personas and plain words | autonomous |
+| F11 | an epic or a story carries a label, or an epic's issue type is not Feature, or a story's is not Story | take the label off, and set the issue type to Feature on an epic and to Story on a story | autonomous |
+
+## Pause and Resume
+
+Steps run top to bottom. On entry, resolve the change issue from start-change's result, check
+the status marker, skip completed steps, reset an in-progress step to pending, and continue.
+Nothing reaches the tracker before Step 6, so a resume before it needs no undo. A resume after
+Step 6 started reads `tracker-record.json` first. It is written after every tracker write, so
+it lists every issue made. Run Step 7 from it before anything else, so the plan file marks
+those issues; when the record reads `ok: false`, a new run then starts at Step 1 and finds them
+(Step 2 sees them as `use`), so no issue is made twice.
+A run that closed HALTED at a stop has nothing to resume: it wrote nothing.
